<title>NORWAY: Amerada makes small gas find off mid-Norwa.</title>
<headline>Amerada makes small gas find off mid-Norwa.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amerada Hess, as operator of licence 197 covering blocks 6306/2 and 6306/5, has found small quantities of gas in an area southwest of the Njord field off mid-Norway, the Norwegian Oil Directorate said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Exploration well 6306/5-1 was drilled to a depth of 2,025 metres below sea level and was permanently plugged and abandoned.</p>
<p>Amerada Hess has a 70 percent interest in licence 197 and state-owned Den norske stats oljeselskap AS 30 percent.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
